# Data and checker definitions for the conjugacy-class action

Untrusted certificate data (`conjTab`, `classOfData`, `classRepsData`, the BFS
tree) and the kernel-cheap Boolean checkers over it. The heavy per-row kernel
`decide`s live in the sibling files `ConjR/Chunk01.lean`–`ConjR/Chunk05.lean`
(one conjugation row each), `ConjAux.lean` (class invariance and row lengths),
and `ConjTree.lean` / `ConjBound.lean` / `ConjCount.lean` (the BFS tree, the
label bound, and the partition counts); the semantic theory is assembled in
`ConjClasses.lean`. Splitting the `decide`s across files keeps each kernel
invocation in its own low-memory process.
-/

